ION_REASON_CODES (operations.py:463) and _LEDGER_GATE_SIGNAL (harness_schemas.py:463).\\n   - hashlib is always imported inside the function that uses it.\\n   - Default values that are evaluated when a part is imported (time.monotonic and time.time) come from parts that import time themselves (streaming.py:7, rate_limits.py:7).\\n   - Typing names the facade no longer imports (List, Tuple, Iterator, Callable) appear only in annotations. The module-level annotation `_ATLAS_NAMESPACE_REGISTRY: Dict[...]` in adapters.py is never evaluated, because of `from __future__ import annotations`.\\n   - The import order changed (audit_rotation is now imported before audit_hmac). This is harmless: audit_rotation imports only os, pathlib and typing.\\n   - The script tools that load the module by file path still work: verify-atlas-binding.py, check_atlas_fpr.py and trading-readonly-escape-hatch.sh. They read _ATLAS_REGISTRY and _ATLAS_NAMESPACE_REGISTRY with getattr after the module runs, and install() has published those names by then.\\n5. Fail direction: unchanged. Each guarded import still falls back to its *_AVAILABLE=False flag. The writer still fails open and breadcrumbs any error. The marker paths keep their deliberate fail-closed returns.\\n6. Python 3.9 and standard library only: no 3.10+ syntax, and the parts import only from the standard library.\\n7. Conditions:\\n   - Condition 5 holds for this package: check_arbitration_kernel.py:312 lists `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*`.\\n   - Condition 7 holds: the audit_emit.py path is unchanged and the logic now lives in _lib/_audit_emit_parts/.\\n   - Adopter delivery: scripts/install.sh:1522-1541 copies each hooks/_lib entry, so the new package ships.\\n\\nP0: none. No declared condition is false against this payload.\\n\\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\\nNone at P1 that is new. One P1 already in the signed lane notes is moved here unchanged: the unbound `line` in _write_event's OSError fallback (codex-p03, writer.py:761)